@orozery  
> Sorry that was the wrong place I mentioned. The keys should be on the spec (as option 2 you mentioned). The values are still derived on the manager.


Adding the label names to the spec adds and additional decision: should the spec labels be the authority or should they just be advisory. As you wanted to support out-of-tree specs, any mismatch between the labels the spec publishes and the labels+values the manager publishes means either the spec is ignored or the manager is ignored, or a best effort merge? To me the spec as authority seems the most "correct", the merge is the most flexible, and the spec keys only as a hint seems unnecessary. Note that a merge will need a gauge re-creation as labels cannot be added to a live gauge.
